WEBVTT


00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.651
Hey, Dad,
did you get
stuck in traffic?


00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.817
How many times
have I told you?
No biking on Sunset.


00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.227
You wanna be some movie
producer's roadkill?


00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.058
I bought you
the Beemer
for a reason.


00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.622
Okay, okay.
I'll drive it.


00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.995
Up the 101 Freeway
to UC Santa Barbara.


00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.094
Dana...


00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.105
Have you even looked
at the catalog I gave you?


00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.670
You're gonna study
fish and surf all day?


00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.232
I can't even talk to you.


00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.802
Hey, you've got
a free ride
to a top school.


00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.778
You're going, case closed.
Why?


00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.840
So I can score
some high-paying job


00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.818
rotting behind
some desk all day
to pay for all this?


00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.082
Okay, maybe "rotting"
was a poor choice.


00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.249
I don't have time for this.


00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.153
You never have time.


00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:10.526
Dad, I appreciate
you work hard,
I really do.


00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.861
But I would suffocate
in that world.


00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.901
I'm like Mom,
I'm too much of
a free spirit.


00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.003
Where did you get that,
"free spirit"?


00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.664
It's from her journal, Dad.


00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.042
You should never have
brought her to LA.


00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.044
This is what
really killed her,
not the cancer.


00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:30.714
Dana, give me a break.
You were five years old,
you barely knew her.


00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.102
High five.


00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.713
It's funny.


00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.452
Get that camera
out of my face.


00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.953
Look at that,
it's right over there.


00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.755
Come on, guys.
Come on, lunch is ready.


00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.628
Daddy,
can I try the camera?


00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.033
Dana,
go get your bucket,
the waves are gonna get it.


00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:28.073
Go get your bucket
out of the sea.


00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.305
This is fun.


00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.488
Look out,
that's a big wave.


00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.691
Come, let's build
a sand castle.


00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.796
I'm gonna get you.
I'm gonna get you.


00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.134
Last night I had a dream


00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.542
where I took my little Dana
back home to South Africa
with me


00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:10.113
and showed her
the Bay of Plenty
and Cave Rock,


00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.576
Vulamanzi Point
and Banana Reef.


00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.885
All the way down
the Wild Coast to
Coffee Bay and Bruce's.


00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.357
Finally we reached
Jeffrey's Bay,


00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:25.591
the one place I've always
dreamed of surfing.


00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:30.092
If only I could
take her there.


00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:35.300
If only she could
see these places, maybe
she could see me, too.


00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.167
But that can
never happen now.


00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.304
I'm out of time.


00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.611
And I'm afraid
I'll never get
back home.


00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.585
Dad, by the time
you get back from
your business trip,


00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.252
I'll be in South Africa.


00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:58.458
I think you and I could
use some time apart.


00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.361
And I think it's time
I learned more about Mom.


00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.128
It's just something
I have to do.


00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:09.472
Don't worry about me.
I'll be fine, as always.
Love, Dana.


00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.653
First trip
to South Africa?


00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.848
Yeah, it is.


00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.050
Visiting family?


00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.149
Um...


00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.284
Kind of.


00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.323
Well, enjoy.


00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.488
Thank you.


00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.625
Let me guess,


00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:42.104
California girl going south
to find winter swell.


00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.066
Is it that obvious?


00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.904
Well, flight to Durban,
surf city.


00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.713
Roxy sunglasses,
ocean hair.


00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:52.012
How very CSI of you.


00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:54.747
Well,
that and The Bomb.


00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.043
Ah!


00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.814
Well, every surfer gets it.
Yeah.


00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.288
I'm Grant.
Dana.


00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.022
Nice to meet you,
California girl.


00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.094
Where you headed?


00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.595
I don't have a plan.


00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.135
Nice.


00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.192
A real beach bum.


00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.961
Yeah.


00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.200
Well, if you make it
down south, look me up.


00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.370
I'll buy you
a smoothie at my bar.


00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.510
It's called
Sally Can't Surf.


00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.379
Cool, thanks.


00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.540
Pleasure.


00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.302
Taxi? Taxi?


00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.472
Miss, where
are you going?


00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.069
Where can I catch
a bus to the beach?


00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.272
There are no buses
today, miss.


00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:56.713
Hey! What are
you doing?


00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:59.315
Special holiday.
Have a good price.


00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:01.444
No problem,
I'll give good price.


00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.587
Attention, passengers.


00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.361
This bus is leaving
for Durban City Beach
in two minutes.


00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.659
Sorry.


00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.595
Move the bag.


00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.469
I'm sorry,
this seat's taken.


00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:22.938
Yeah? Who takes it?


00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:24.771
Her.


00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:28.612
Hey, you're late.
I saved you a seat.


00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.663
Pushy.


00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.667
I'll say.
What a creep.


00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.335
I mean,
my name is Pushy.


00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:53.828
Oh.


00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:57.308
That's unusual.
What does it mean
in your language?


00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.645
Pushy.
Like "pushy"?


00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.870
Actually, my Zulu
name is Nokuthula.


00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.074
Which means...


00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.681
"Be quiet."


00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.628
What?


00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:29.564
Never seen a white girl
riding the bus before.


00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:32.167
Well, I've never seen
a black girl who surfs.


00:08:32.245 --> 00:08:33.439
Well, if you're lucky,


00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:36.414
maybe you'll get
a chance to observe it
for the first time.


00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.550
Maybe you'll
learn something.


00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:41.746
Well, if that
particular scenario
presents itself,


00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:46.349
don't be surprised
if I'm not the one
who gets schooled.


00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.429
That's New Pier.


00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:28.695
She throws killer sets
almost every day.


00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:33.428
Best spot in the city.


00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:34.700
Let's do it.


00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.509
You cool?
Yeah, I'll see you there.


00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:03.726
Looks decent.


00:10:03.803 --> 00:10:04.827
Decent?


00:10:05.338 --> 00:10:07.772
Better than Malibu,
I bet.


00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:11.269
My advice to you
is to sit wide,


00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.508
smile, wait for
a wrap-around set


00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:17.347
and maybe you'll catch
a little ride.


00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.846
Shit.


00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:23.115
What?


00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:25.417
Don't tell me you're afraid
of 4-foot waves.


00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:29.222
No, it's not the waves,
it's her. Tara.


00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.863
Wow, Tara can surf.


00:10:41.774 --> 00:10:44.402
So, what do we do,
just jump in?


00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:48.403
Sometimes it's the only way.


00:11:19.812 --> 00:11:22.144
It's mobbed enough out here,
go surf South Beach.


00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:25.747
There's plenty ofwaves
out here, Tara.


00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:29.914
Yeah, for me.
Not you,
or Barbie there.


00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:32.922
Hey, you stay out of my way
and I'll stay out of yours.


00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:35.893
Yeah? You better
explain the pecking order
to her, Push.


00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:37.887
Hate to have
to educate her
the hard way.


00:11:44.937 --> 00:11:47.269
Let's go. I hate
this aggro vibe.


00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:52.673
Hell, no. I just flew
23 hours in coach.
I'm surfing.


00:12:02.188 --> 00:12:04.053
Gidget alert.
Coming through.


00:12:05.024 --> 00:12:07.492
You here for
your surf lesson?


00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.653
Hey, Baywatch,
how you doing?


00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.357
Did your daddy buy you
an antique surf board?


00:12:39.391 --> 00:12:40.449
I got it.


00:12:41.927 --> 00:12:43.519
No, you don't.


00:13:31.343 --> 00:13:33.811
Wow.
Yeah, it was a nice wave.


00:13:34.046 --> 00:13:37.777
No, I mean, whoa,
you stole one from
the queen bee.


00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.784
Talk about getting schooled.


00:13:39.952 --> 00:13:43.080
Yeah, Tara needs to
loosen her sphincter up.


00:13:43.155 --> 00:13:45.555
Let's go.


00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:56.197
Great. Now every knob
thinks they can surf.


00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:03.103
Outside!


00:14:05.277 --> 00:14:06.608
Out of the way, Barbie.


00:14:10.149 --> 00:14:11.241
Move!


00:14:11.684 --> 00:14:13.777
Hey, I said
I had it. Hey!


00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:16.286
Shit!


00:14:36.108 --> 00:14:37.939
What do you think
you were doing?
Shit!


00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.308
You could have killed me!
Get out of the water,
you idiot!


00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:41.910
You dropped in
on her, Tara!


00:14:45.584 --> 00:14:46.573
Damn it!


00:14:46.652 --> 00:14:47.983
Why do you have
to be such a...


00:14:48.053 --> 00:14:49.953
Such a what?
God!


00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:52.354
That's right. Run away.


00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.620
And don't come back!


00:15:03.502 --> 00:15:04.992
Is that how it is
in South Africa?


00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.501
Screw her.


00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:09.541
You snagged the barrel
of the day out there.
Right in their faces.


00:15:09.675 --> 00:15:11.165
Yeah, but I busted
my board!


00:15:11.377 --> 00:15:13.106
Better the board
than your head.


00:15:13.812 --> 00:15:16.645
It was my mom's.
I can't replace it.


00:15:22.254 --> 00:15:24.051
I can't believe it!


00:15:28.727 --> 00:15:31.662
No. No, no.


00:15:41.807 --> 00:15:43.638
This can't be happening.


00:15:47.579 --> 00:15:48.739
Shit.


00:15:48.814 --> 00:15:50.111
Your money?


00:15:50.182 --> 00:15:51.240
I don't care about that.


00:15:52.985 --> 00:15:54.509
My mother's carving's gone.


00:15:55.154 --> 00:15:57.452
Yeah. These lockers
are pretty flimsy.


00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.917
Really?


00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:05.692
You know what?
I'm sorry.


00:16:05.764 --> 00:16:07.823
Can you just
leave me alone?
Please?


00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:34.250
Dana, give me a break.
You barely knew her.


00:16:39.164 --> 00:16:42.395
Hi, I'd like
to make a collect call
to the United States.


00:16:44.803 --> 00:16:49.001
Area code 310-467...


00:16:49.775 --> 00:16:52.437
You must be hungry.


00:16:52.878 --> 00:16:54.971
We're grilling
a fish tonight.


00:17:00.085 --> 00:17:01.575
Hang up.


00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:05.414
Come on, give it
one more chance.


00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.020
What kind of fish?


00:17:18.637 --> 00:17:22.198
My dad would freak
if he saw me doing this.


00:17:22.274 --> 00:17:25.505
He would drag me
home for sure.


00:17:25.577 --> 00:17:28.375
Well, if he knew
where I was.


00:17:28.447 --> 00:17:30.677
Your dad doesn't know
you're in Africa?


00:17:31.316 --> 00:17:34.217
Oh, man. You are
in trouble, girl.


00:17:36.321 --> 00:17:41.224
No, I doubt that.
I'm actually not sure
he even knows I'm gone.


00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:42.585
What?


00:17:47.266 --> 00:17:49.063
Thanks, man.


00:17:49.168 --> 00:17:50.692
Thank you.
Cheers.


00:18:03.982 --> 00:18:06.416
This is where
you live?


00:18:06.485 --> 00:18:07.509
Yes.


00:18:07.686 --> 00:18:09.677
And these people
are my family.


00:18:09.755 --> 00:18:10.779
Hey, guys.
Hi.


00:18:11.557 --> 00:18:14.151
This might
be paradise.


00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:17.491
Wait a minute.
What the hell is
she doing here?


00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:18.791
Uh...


00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:19.956
She lives here.


00:18:20.032 --> 00:18:21.056
What?


00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:26.303
She lives with you?
All right, strike
"paradise," insert "hell."


00:18:26.738 --> 00:18:28.501
What is her deal anyway?


00:18:28.574 --> 00:18:31.338
For starters, she's
a professional athlete.


00:18:31.577 --> 00:18:33.602
She's the number one
on the Roxy team,


00:18:33.679 --> 00:18:35.579
and she doesn't let
anyone forget it.


00:18:35.647 --> 00:18:38.115
I thought I said something
about "don't come back."


00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.374
Yet here you are again,
like a bad memory.


00:18:40.452 --> 00:18:42.511
It's not just
your house, Tara.


00:18:42.588 --> 00:18:45.648
No, but there's
a pecking order,
just like the line-up.


00:18:45.724 --> 00:18:48.522
Yeah, well,
your pecking order
doesn't work for me.


00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:52.688
Cops are back.
You know what to do.


00:18:52.764 --> 00:18:54.789
Not again.
We'll take this up later.


00:18:56.368 --> 00:18:58.029
Come on.
TARA: Let's go!


00:19:12.017 --> 00:19:13.314
Come on.


00:19:15.754 --> 00:19:19.315
By order of the
eThekwini Metropolitan
Municipality,


00:19:19.391 --> 00:19:21.518
this property is condemned


00:19:21.693 --> 00:19:23.957
and must be
vacated immediately.


00:19:24.363 --> 00:19:25.523
Care to fill me in?


00:19:25.597 --> 00:19:26.825
They want us out of here.


00:19:27.499 --> 00:19:29.126
We're a nuisance.


00:19:30.369 --> 00:19:32.303
They really want to
tear the place down.


00:19:35.374 --> 00:19:37.239
This is your final warning.


00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:40.137
This structure
will be demolished
in one week.


00:19:42.114 --> 00:19:45.242
By order of the court,
this is your final warning.


00:19:51.123 --> 00:19:52.715
Piss balloons.
Oh!


00:19:53.759 --> 00:19:54.919
Disgusting!


00:19:58.397 --> 00:20:01.924
This is your last warning.
You have one week to get out.


00:20:04.336 --> 00:20:06.770
Come on,
I'll introduce you
to the family.


00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.765
We laid claim to
this beach years ago.


00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:14.178
At first it was
just a couple of tents
and some surf boards.


00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.105
Now it's
a self-sustaining
community.


00:20:17.182 --> 00:20:22.210
Really, it's just a bunch of
friends who are serious about
goofing off and riding waves.


00:20:22.354 --> 00:20:24.117
Welcome.
I like your family.


00:20:24.289 --> 00:20:27.850
Best people in the world.
I met them all through Tim.


00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.818
Hey!


00:20:30.696 --> 00:20:31.685
Whoa!


00:20:32.698 --> 00:20:34.563
Speak of the devil.


00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:36.123
Timothy, say hi to Dana.


00:20:36.535 --> 00:20:37.866
Hey.
Hi.


00:20:39.738 --> 00:20:40.727
You from LA?


00:20:40.806 --> 00:20:42.933
Yeah. I got in today.


00:20:43.242 --> 00:20:44.231
You staying?


00:20:44.309 --> 00:20:45.401
I don't know.


00:20:45.877 --> 00:20:47.538
That means you're staying.


00:20:47.613 --> 00:20:50.639
Okay, Pushy,
let's show her
the best part.


00:20:56.421 --> 00:20:57.786
You all right?


00:20:57.956 --> 00:20:59.548
My humble abode.


00:21:00.993 --> 00:21:04.019
Cool. Does it run?


00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:06.724
If I have my way,
it will. Someday.


00:21:08.967 --> 00:21:10.594
That's lots of elephants.


00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:13.103
Yeah, I volunteer at
the nature reserve.


00:21:13.639 --> 00:21:16.972
In between being one of
the best board shapers around.


00:21:17.042 --> 00:21:20.808
And our go-to fix-it man.
Hence the mess.


00:21:21.613 --> 00:21:23.979
But I can move some
of this stuff if you
need a place to stay.


00:21:24.049 --> 00:21:27.314
Nice try!
She's staying with me.


00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:30.516
Come on.


00:21:43.602 --> 00:21:47.504
Careful, Dana,
you've seen how we deal
with blow-ins around here.


00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:48.997
She's staying
with me, Tara.


00:21:50.942 --> 00:21:52.876
Just stay out of my way.


00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:55.742
My pleasure.


00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:04.553
So, it's not the Hilton,
but it's not so bad.


00:22:07.759 --> 00:22:09.590
Yeah, I could hang
with this for a while.


00:22:13.865 --> 00:22:14.889
Ha!


00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:18.868
I see Laura and Sally,
all the top Roxy riders,


00:22:20.272 --> 00:22:22.502
but I don't see Tara.


00:22:22.574 --> 00:22:24.565
I must have
missed her somehow.


00:22:24.643 --> 00:22:26.008
Uh-huh.


00:22:26.078 --> 00:22:28.444
Girl has it made, hey?


00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:31.346
Travel the world,
surf killer waves all day,


00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:34.385
pose for the cameras
and get paid for it.


00:22:34.686 --> 00:22:36.881
Why don't you try
out for the team?
I did.


00:22:38.223 --> 00:22:39.520
Didn't make the cut.


00:22:39.591 --> 00:22:41.786
Why? You can rip,
I saw you.


00:22:42.494 --> 00:22:44.587
Or...
Or?


00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:49.233
Or Tara screwed me over.


00:22:50.235 --> 00:22:53.068
Wow. Well, I wouldn't
put it past her.


00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:57.539
Yeah, one big,
happy family.


00:22:57.609 --> 00:22:59.577
That's what we are.


00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:04.005
You jet-lagged?


00:23:04.082 --> 00:23:05.242
Maybe a little.


00:23:18.163 --> 00:23:19.562
Dana?


00:23:41.386 --> 00:23:42.444
Dana!


00:24:09.948 --> 00:24:12.280
Hey, sister!


00:24:13.418 --> 00:24:15.648
Okay, be cool.


00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:16.744
I am cool.


00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:18.813
No, be cool.


00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:19.948
Okay.


00:24:20.025 --> 00:24:21.993
Look, it's a zombie.


00:24:22.394 --> 00:24:24.521
Night of the living Dana.


00:24:24.596 --> 00:24:27.121
Food. Give me food.


00:24:27.599 --> 00:24:29.032
Voila.
Whoo!


00:24:31.303 --> 00:24:34.966
Oh, my God. That's, like,
the best fish I've ever had.


00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:37.099
Well, that's good,
'cause it's the
main course tomorrow.


00:24:37.175 --> 00:24:39.109
And the next night.
And breakfast.


00:24:40.846 --> 00:24:42.336
Nice.


00:24:46.418 --> 00:24:48.579
Hey. Grant.
Hey.


00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:51.918
Hey, Sugaree.


00:24:54.392 --> 00:24:55.654
I don't believe it.


00:24:56.127 --> 00:24:57.389
You know Grant?


00:24:57.462 --> 00:24:59.293
I met him
on the plane,
briefly.


00:25:00.765 --> 00:25:02.630
Fifty bucks says
he was flying first class.


00:25:02.701 --> 00:25:03.827
How do you know?


00:25:04.503 --> 00:25:06.630
Grant's the only one
that can afford
a truck like that.


00:25:07.906 --> 00:25:09.237
I wish I had one.


00:25:09.574 --> 00:25:12.065
TlM: Trust me,
you don't want to
get mixed up in that.


00:25:12.477 --> 00:25:14.775
Come on, I'll show you
the giant sea turtles.


00:25:14.846 --> 00:25:16.575
They lay their eggs
just up the beach.


00:25:16.815 --> 00:25:18.043
California girl!


00:25:19.684 --> 00:25:21.652
I had a feeling you'd
show up before long.


00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:23.051
Small world, huh?


00:25:23.288 --> 00:25:25.552
Yeah.
Pushy brought me here.


00:25:26.558 --> 00:25:27.820
Oh, Pushy.


00:25:30.095 --> 00:25:31.494
Bro.


00:25:31.863 --> 00:25:33.125
I owe you one.
I do, I do.


00:25:34.466 --> 00:25:36.957
So, California girl,
are you gonna show us
what you got?


00:25:38.069 --> 00:25:39.866
I don't know.
Come on.


00:25:40.305 --> 00:25:42.136
You feel the groove.


00:25:44.042 --> 00:25:45.509
Come on. Come on.


00:25:46.978 --> 00:25:48.639
Can you hold this?


00:25:55.720 --> 00:25:59.747
"Let me show you
the giant sea turtles"?
Seriously?


00:26:00.158 --> 00:26:01.216
Shut up.


00:26:19.878 --> 00:26:21.869
California girl can dance.


00:27:33.885 --> 00:27:35.512
Pushy?


00:28:10.488 --> 00:28:12.046
See ya.


00:28:25.637 --> 00:28:27.502
Morning, California girl!


00:28:27.806 --> 00:28:28.898
Hey.


00:28:29.541 --> 00:28:30.599
Jet-lagged?


00:28:30.675 --> 00:28:31.699
I'm here, aren't l?


00:28:36.815 --> 00:28:40.046
Can't believe
those two are friends.
They seem so different.


00:28:40.885 --> 00:28:43.513
The love of the ocean
brings different
spirits together.


00:28:45.023 --> 00:28:47.924
I think they might
both love something
else, too.


00:28:48.993 --> 00:28:50.426
I'm not going there.


00:28:50.495 --> 00:28:51.655
Oh, yeah?


00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:54.028
Think I might have
seen your lips
go there last night.


00:28:55.333 --> 00:28:58.359
Maybe a little
tongue, too.
Right.


00:29:00.338 --> 00:29:04.001
Go ahead, girl.
You got this.
Show 'em what you got.


00:29:04.075 --> 00:29:06.407
I'm all over it.


00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:11.414
Go for it,
California girl!


00:29:15.153 --> 00:29:16.984
Whoo!


00:29:17.055 --> 00:29:18.750
Go, girl!


00:29:28.833 --> 00:29:30.892
Keep up, old man.
I'm trying!


00:29:41.946 --> 00:29:44.881
Go get 'em, Tim.


00:30:15.914 --> 00:30:18.075
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go!


00:30:27.058 --> 00:30:28.582
Yeah!


00:31:15.373 --> 00:31:16.362
Whoo!


00:31:30.989 --> 00:31:32.786
You don't
remember her at all?


00:31:35.526 --> 00:31:39.223
Just a few blurry images.
You know, like in a dream.


00:31:39.297 --> 00:31:41.458
Her name was Catherine.


00:31:41.532 --> 00:31:43.830
I was five years old.


00:31:43.902 --> 00:31:44.926
TlM: Those are all
you have left?


00:31:45.503 --> 00:31:49.769
And there was another
keepsake of hers, but
it got stolen with my stuff.


00:31:50.808 --> 00:31:53.038
She always wanted
to show me her homeland.


00:31:55.046 --> 00:31:56.877
Your mom was a hottie!


00:31:59.150 --> 00:32:00.777
Well, like mother
like daughter.


00:32:04.422 --> 00:32:05.446
Oh!


00:32:05.523 --> 00:32:08.321
Yes. Check it, bro.


00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:12.220
Classic Supertubes.
And not a soul out.


00:32:13.164 --> 00:32:15.359
When was the last time
you saw J-bay like that?


00:32:15.833 --> 00:32:17.198
Never.
Never.


00:32:17.268 --> 00:32:19.259
She wrote
about Jeffrey's Bay
a lot in her journal.


00:32:19.504 --> 00:32:20.835
Like it was
someplace sacred.


00:32:21.105 --> 00:32:24.472
Sacred's the word.
Finest point break
in the world.


00:32:25.076 --> 00:32:27.442
My old stomping grounds.


00:32:27.512 --> 00:32:29.742
Oh! When J-bay fires
on all cylinders...


00:32:30.114 --> 00:32:31.945
And the tubes are grinding
from the Boneyards,


00:32:32.016 --> 00:32:34.041
through lmpossibles
right down to The Point...


00:32:34.419 --> 00:32:36.250
The holy grail
of right-handers.


00:32:36.321 --> 00:32:37.379
The holy grail.


00:32:37.555 --> 00:32:40.149
She said it was
the one place that she had
to surf before she died.


00:32:40.458 --> 00:32:41.652
But she never did.


00:32:42.794 --> 00:32:44.421
No.
Probably couldn't.


00:32:45.396 --> 00:32:46.693
But I will.


00:32:46.764 --> 00:32:48.197
I'm gonna surf it for her.


00:32:49.067 --> 00:32:50.091
You know what else?


00:32:50.234 --> 00:32:53.169
I'm going to go to
every one of those
places in those photos.


00:32:54.339 --> 00:32:57.536
Do you know what, Dana?
You're on Uhambo.


00:32:58.276 --> 00:33:00.369
That's what we call it
in South Africa.


00:33:00.511 --> 00:33:02.945
It's like when
someone's looking for...


00:33:04.515 --> 00:33:05.539
What?


00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:08.778
I don't know.
My mom, I guess.


00:33:09.387 --> 00:33:11.048
Or maybe yourself.


00:33:11.122 --> 00:33:13.215
In Australia
they call it
a walkabout.


00:33:13.658 --> 00:33:15.455
In the Holy Land,
a pilgrimage.


00:33:15.526 --> 00:33:17.721
What do you call it
in America?


00:33:18.129 --> 00:33:19.824
Um...


00:33:19.897 --> 00:33:21.990
A journey?
Boring.


00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:23.590
Don't like it.
Don't like it.


00:33:26.571 --> 00:33:27.663
An odyssey?


00:33:28.639 --> 00:33:29.765
Yes.
I like that.


00:33:30.208 --> 00:33:31.971
An odyssey.


00:33:32.043 --> 00:33:34.341
I call it a pipe dream.


00:33:36.981 --> 00:33:39.541
You think it's still
Endless Summer out there?


00:33:39.617 --> 00:33:42.381
It's a long, hard trip
down the Wild Coast
before you get to J-bay.


00:33:43.287 --> 00:33:45.380
Not to mention
winter's coming. Do you
even have a wetsuit?


00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:48.391
Then it's sharks
in the ocean,


00:33:48.659 --> 00:33:52.186
Iocals who demand
total respect, and
a heavy, heavy wave.


00:33:53.297 --> 00:33:55.595
Beverly Hills girl here
wouldn't last a day
on her own.


00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:57.925
Who says she's on
her own, Tara?


00:33:59.804 --> 00:34:03.900
Dana, you and l
are going on this
odyssey together.


00:34:04.042 --> 00:34:06.476
That's good,
the blind leading the blind.


00:34:08.279 --> 00:34:09.439
I say they pull it off.


00:34:10.214 --> 00:34:13.047
Hundred bucks says
they don't.
And I want evidence.


00:34:13.518 --> 00:34:15.918
Pictures ofyou
at all those places.
And surfing them.


00:34:16.788 --> 00:34:18.255
Of course.
You're on.


00:34:18.322 --> 00:34:19.380
She'll never
surf J-bay.


00:34:20.591 --> 00:34:21.956
I could
lend you my truck.


00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:24.018
Really?


00:34:24.128 --> 00:34:27.120
At a price.
You ever waited tables?


00:34:28.666 --> 00:34:29.928
One of my waiters just quit.


00:34:30.635 --> 00:34:33.297
Maybe Pushy can show you
the ropes here.


00:34:35.673 --> 00:34:37.766
Sound good?
Sounds good.


00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:40.134
All right.


00:34:44.916 --> 00:34:46.474
Spare set.


00:34:48.519 --> 00:34:50.783
Always be prepared.


00:34:50.855 --> 00:34:52.482
It's a Land Rover.


00:34:52.557 --> 00:34:54.684
You drive it hard,
you put it away wet.


00:34:54.759 --> 00:34:56.158
We can do that.


00:35:03.734 --> 00:35:06.464
Thanks, Grant.
You sure you don't
want to come with us?


00:35:07.772 --> 00:35:12.004
Nah.
We can go for a spin later,
perhaps, when you get back.


00:35:12.910 --> 00:35:15.276
Midnight, maybe.
Just you and me.


00:35:15.346 --> 00:35:16.813
You're not that lucky.


00:35:19.917 --> 00:35:21.942
Here you go.
Document your
odyssey properly.


00:35:22.286 --> 00:35:24.720
Tim, where did you find
a Polaroid camera?


00:35:24.922 --> 00:35:27.152
Junk shop in Durban.
Dug up some film as well.


00:35:29.160 --> 00:35:31.651
That is so sweet of you.


00:35:31.729 --> 00:35:33.720
I got one more thing.


00:35:43.307 --> 00:35:45.298
Tim, this is amazing.


00:35:45.877 --> 00:35:48.846
Do you know how few people
can fix a board like this?


00:35:51.749 --> 00:35:53.114
Aw!


00:35:53.184 --> 00:35:56.415
You fixed her board, dude,
and you just got cheek.


00:35:59.957 --> 00:36:01.015
Be careful.


00:36:01.392 --> 00:36:02.859
Tara may be half-joking,


00:36:02.927 --> 00:36:05.122
but there's
a lot of bad things that
can happen out there.


00:36:05.196 --> 00:36:06.720
You have a long highway
ahead of you.


00:36:07.465 --> 00:36:10.491
Life is a highway


00:36:10.568 --> 00:36:11.967
Thank you.


00:36:13.504 --> 00:36:16.940
I wanna ride it
All night long


00:36:26.517 --> 00:36:29.008
Life is a highway


00:36:29.086 --> 00:36:32.817
I wanna ride it all night long


00:36:33.624 --> 00:36:35.251
Yeah!


00:36:35.560 --> 00:36:38.324
If you're goin' my way


00:36:38.396 --> 00:36:41.888
I wanna drive it
all night long


00:36:49.307 --> 00:36:54.176
"And I reached it
just as dawn broke,
my favorite time of the day.


00:36:55.379 --> 00:36:58.837
"Difficult to find,
almost impossible
to leave."


00:37:01.886 --> 00:37:03.547
That is some poetic shit.


00:37:04.021 --> 00:37:05.886
I mean, that's deep.


00:37:05.957 --> 00:37:07.015
Think so?


00:37:09.393 --> 00:37:12.556
Sounds like she was
a first-rate mom.


00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:13.688
She was.


00:37:15.733 --> 00:37:18.167
At least I think she was.


00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:20.669
I mean, I know
she was a free spirit.


00:37:23.874 --> 00:37:27.469
Shit, all I know is
what's in that book.


00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:33.280
In the memorable words
of my dad,
"l barely even knew her."


00:37:33.651 --> 00:37:35.846
You know, I bet
you are a lot like her.


00:37:36.287 --> 00:37:38.221
I hope so.


00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:42.388
I live every day
with the fear that
I'll never know.


00:37:46.831 --> 00:37:49.095
Yes. I can see it.


00:37:50.735 --> 00:37:52.032
See what?


00:37:54.505 --> 00:37:55.597
There it is!


00:38:01.312 --> 00:38:02.745
It's a Land Rover.


00:38:03.281 --> 00:38:06.478
Like Grant said,
you drive it hard
and put it away wet.


00:38:06.550 --> 00:38:07.539
Whoo!


00:38:08.552 --> 00:38:09.678
Yeah!


00:38:22.733 --> 00:38:23.825
Hello.


00:38:24.535 --> 00:38:26.662
Well, that was rude.


00:39:56.694 --> 00:39:59.390
Looks pretty
free-spirited to me.


00:40:15.546 --> 00:40:17.514
Yeah.


00:40:23.087 --> 00:40:27.285
Dana and Pushy's odyssey,
step one, complete.


00:40:29.760 --> 00:40:31.352
Put it away wet.


00:40:38.269 --> 00:40:40.430
Hey, man,
put it away wet.


00:40:45.776 --> 00:40:46.936
Hole in the Wall.


00:40:47.011 --> 00:40:48.205
Done.


00:40:48.312 --> 00:40:50.246
Cha-ching, baby.


00:40:50.314 --> 00:40:51.838
Don't count
your pennies
just yet.


00:41:00.257 --> 00:41:03.852
The rule around here
is the new girl
cleans the toilet.


00:41:04.328 --> 00:41:05.727
Oh, come on.


00:41:05.796 --> 00:41:07.559
Relax, it's not so bad.


00:41:07.631 --> 00:41:11.158
Except when some oke
barks the dog after too
many klippies and coke.


00:41:11.969 --> 00:41:13.869
A what?
You know,
parks a tiger.


00:41:14.605 --> 00:41:15.629
Blows chunks.


00:41:15.706 --> 00:41:17.606
Oh! Gross.


00:41:18.509 --> 00:41:19.601
And by the way,


00:41:19.677 --> 00:41:22.703
just in case you were
wondering what's in
this odyssey for me...


00:41:23.414 --> 00:41:24.972
I was waiting for this.


00:41:25.049 --> 00:41:28.177
In exchange for being
your trusty guide,


00:41:28.252 --> 00:41:31.915
you will teach me
how to pull off
your 360 floater.


00:41:32.523 --> 00:41:34.150
You're gonna try out
for the Roxy team again?


00:41:34.925 --> 00:41:36.893
You are not the only
girl on a mission.


00:41:39.196 --> 00:41:41.687
Hell, yeah.
Here.


00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:45.864
This is Spike
from Wakescape
with your swell update.


00:41:45.970 --> 00:41:48.803
That frothy low
that's been spinning
off Antarctica


00:41:48.873 --> 00:41:51.398
has intensified over
the last 24 hours.


00:41:51.675 --> 00:41:53.370
If it keeps
spinning like that,


00:41:53.444 --> 00:41:55.207
we're due for
a macking southerly
groundswell


00:41:55.279 --> 00:41:58.806
to hit the East Coast,
so you guys in J-bay
better start waxing up.


00:41:59.250 --> 00:42:01.081
And now back to music...
You hear that, Flash?


00:42:01.151 --> 00:42:04.348
J-bay is gonna be
all time, bro.


00:42:04.855 --> 00:42:06.254
Screwdriver.


00:42:06.857 --> 00:42:10.258
Thank you.
Fix the radio, man?


00:42:26.210 --> 00:42:30.237
Walk this way.
Straight. On foot only.


00:42:30.514 --> 00:42:31.845
Thank you.


00:42:51.468 --> 00:42:53.868
Long way in, hey?


00:42:56.974 --> 00:42:58.669
Uh... Pushy?


00:43:05.516 --> 00:43:08.144
I guess we should
step aside.


00:43:08.218 --> 00:43:09.708
Yeah, seems wise.


00:43:29.373 --> 00:43:32.604
Your mom went to
some pretty far-out places.


00:43:32.676 --> 00:43:34.837
Yeah, like Beverly Hills.


00:43:39.984 --> 00:43:44.250
You know,
maybe that old guy
was yanking our chain.


00:43:46.357 --> 00:43:50.123
Or maybe he wasn't.


00:43:52.396 --> 00:43:55.297
This is why surfers
invent words.


00:43:55.366 --> 00:43:56.424
Invent words?


00:43:56.934 --> 00:43:59.402
You know, like
"gnarly" or "stoked."


00:43:59.470 --> 00:44:00.459
Huh!


00:44:00.871 --> 00:44:03.738
So, what do we do,
just jump in?


00:44:04.441 --> 00:44:06.170
Sure, you go first.


00:44:19.089 --> 00:44:22.718
Okay, the aerial 360.
Watch and learn.


00:44:39.143 --> 00:44:41.043
Go for it, Push!
Come on!


00:44:47.317 --> 00:44:49.217
You're good. Try again!


00:45:03.200 --> 00:45:06.397
Look, because
you ride goofy you have to
nail this on your backhand.


00:45:07.071 --> 00:45:09.005
It's a lot harder, Push.


00:45:09.073 --> 00:45:10.404
No kidding.


00:45:10.974 --> 00:45:12.965
You're gonna go down,
round and up.


00:46:13.237 --> 00:46:15.432
From the flight deck
this is Captain Glen Ross.


00:46:15.639 --> 00:46:18.164
We're beginning our final
descent into Durban.


00:46:18.242 --> 00:46:19.607
Please fasten
your seat belts,


00:46:19.676 --> 00:46:21.701
we'll be landing
in 10 minutes.


00:46:26.283 --> 00:46:28.911
Mango smoothie,
easy on the ice, Push.


00:46:34.124 --> 00:46:36.183
Look. Dana,
I think we just got off
on the wrong foot.


00:46:36.260 --> 00:46:37.352
Mmm-hmm.


00:46:37.427 --> 00:46:38.894
'Cause believe it or not,
I'm kind of rooting for you.


00:46:39.329 --> 00:46:41.923
What, like you were
rooting for Pushy to
join the Roxy team?


00:46:42.900 --> 00:46:44.162
She told you
I sabotaged her?


00:46:45.769 --> 00:46:48.260
Yeah, that's bullshit.
The truth is,
she surfed like crap.


00:46:49.873 --> 00:46:52.307
I was there.
She was out of shape
and unprepared.


00:46:53.710 --> 00:46:56.201
Come on, you know it
takes hard work and
commitment to be on a team.


00:46:56.280 --> 00:46:58.180
Some people have it,
some people don't.


00:46:59.049 --> 00:47:02.018
I think you might
have it, Dana. Might.


00:47:02.986 --> 00:47:05.113
There's an open tryout
in Jeffrey's Bay
next Saturday.


00:47:05.189 --> 00:47:06.520
And since you're headed
that way anyway...


00:47:06.590 --> 00:47:08.524
Yeah, it's not
my scene, Tara.


00:47:08.592 --> 00:47:09.650
But Pushy will be there.


00:47:12.796 --> 00:47:15.287
Sweet. So will l.
Good.


00:47:17.467 --> 00:47:19.697
That's for you, Push.
Don't work too hard.


00:47:24.875 --> 00:47:26.843
Even if I do
make it to J-bay,


00:47:26.910 --> 00:47:28.502
she'll never let me
make the team.


00:47:28.579 --> 00:47:31.173
Well, maybe that decision's
up to you and not her.


00:47:50.634 --> 00:47:52.124
What?


00:48:06.283 --> 00:48:07.443
Hey.


00:48:07.517 --> 00:48:09.007
Who was that?
Who?


00:48:10.153 --> 00:48:12.178
The guy in the truck.


00:48:12.256 --> 00:48:16.955
Just some oke asking about
the surf here.
He didn't even have a stick.


00:48:17.027 --> 00:48:18.289
So, you don't know him?


00:48:18.362 --> 00:48:20.523
Nah. Never seen
him before.


00:48:22.432 --> 00:48:23.421
Mmm.


00:48:26.737 --> 00:48:28.329
Pushy,


00:48:29.640 --> 00:48:31.938
I think I just saw
the guy who stole my stuff.


00:48:32.809 --> 00:48:35.710
What? You sure?
You only saw him once.


00:48:36.313 --> 00:48:40.249
Pushy, I need to get
my mom's stuff back.


00:48:40.450 --> 00:48:43.442
What's so important
about this stuff anyway?


00:48:43.520 --> 00:48:45.078
I mean, I know it was
your mom's, but...


00:48:45.155 --> 00:48:48.181
It just... It just is.


00:48:50.961 --> 00:48:54.021
Tell you what.
Shift's almost over.


00:48:54.097 --> 00:48:56.429
Go home.
I'll cover for you.


00:48:57.134 --> 00:48:58.601
Thanks, Push.


00:49:00.270 --> 00:49:02.135
Tim.


00:49:02.205 --> 00:49:03.229
Hey.


00:49:03.774 --> 00:49:05.935
How's the odyssey coming?
It's coming.


00:49:06.009 --> 00:49:08.000
Yeah?
Yeah. I'm just waiting
on the water now.


00:49:08.078 --> 00:49:10.273
Yeah, I'm tracking
that for you.


00:49:10.380 --> 00:49:12.575
You still got a couple of days
before the big swell comes.


00:49:13.383 --> 00:49:14.748
Thanks.
No problem.


00:49:16.153 --> 00:49:17.347
What?


00:49:18.188 --> 00:49:19.655
What?


00:49:20.223 --> 00:49:22.248
Is it me, or do you
smell like an elephant?


00:49:22.326 --> 00:49:24.692
Hey! Elephants don't smell.


00:49:25.495 --> 00:49:28.157
That's pure man-sweat
you're taking in.


00:49:30.167 --> 00:49:32.362
So, you had a long day
at the reserve, I smell.


00:49:32.836 --> 00:49:34.360
Long but good.


00:49:34.438 --> 00:49:36.133
You wanna see some pictures
while I get cleaned up?


00:49:36.206 --> 00:49:37.298
Sure.
Yeah?


00:49:45.248 --> 00:49:47.273
See the way they
take care of one another?


00:49:47.351 --> 00:49:49.876
Looking after the old ones,
sick ones, young ones.


00:49:50.220 --> 00:49:52.848
I heard they even mourn
when one of them dies.


00:49:53.190 --> 00:49:56.250
Yeah, yeah,
I've seen that.
Unfortunately.


00:49:56.793 --> 00:49:58.556
You lost one?


00:49:58.628 --> 00:50:02.189
Rare, but we do have
some poachers around here.


00:50:03.333 --> 00:50:04.391
Shit.


00:50:04.468 --> 00:50:05.628
Gotta hand it
to 'em, though.


00:50:05.936 --> 00:50:09.463
After they mourn
they just close ranks,


00:50:09.906 --> 00:50:12.204
the family reorders itself
and they just move on.


00:50:13.844 --> 00:50:14.970
Is that why
you're drawn to them?


00:50:15.545 --> 00:50:16.842
What do you mean?


00:50:16.913 --> 00:50:19.677
You know, the family thing.


00:50:19.950 --> 00:50:23.386
Kind of like what
you've created here.


00:50:25.389 --> 00:50:26.378
Huh.


00:50:28.191 --> 00:50:30.523
Well, aren't you
a smart girl.


00:50:30.594 --> 00:50:31.959
Mmm.


00:50:32.029 --> 00:50:34.088
Not so smart.


00:50:35.098 --> 00:50:37.999
I'm probably the last person
you should be listening to.


00:50:39.669 --> 00:50:42.001
Hey, where
are you going?


00:50:42.339 --> 00:50:44.102
You're not the only one
that has to shower.


00:50:44.174 --> 00:50:46.074
Got a hot date tonight.


00:50:46.143 --> 00:50:49.078
I'm going dancing
with Pushy.


00:50:51.181 --> 00:50:53.342
Hey, let me know
about that swell.


00:51:04.528 --> 00:51:06.553
First time in Durban, sir?


00:51:06.630 --> 00:51:09.428
Well, first time
in about 20 years.


00:51:31.888 --> 00:51:33.150
Hey, sister.


00:51:33.223 --> 00:51:34.315
Hi.


00:51:34.658 --> 00:51:37.286
This is it.
This is where I grew up.


00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:40.420
And it's the best spot for
kwaito music and dancing.


00:52:08.125 --> 00:52:09.353
Careful, sister.


00:52:09.659 --> 00:52:12.253
Come on. You never seen
a white girl dance before?


00:52:12.896 --> 00:52:16.127
I'm teaching you my moves,
show me some of yours.


00:52:19.035 --> 00:52:21.765
Okay, then.
Watch how it's done.


00:52:25.408 --> 00:52:26.932
Go, sister!


00:52:49.332 --> 00:52:52.597
Hello, everyone. Let's
kick it in here all night.
You're ready?


00:53:36.813 --> 00:53:39.805
Why are you here?
What the hell do you
want in my business?


00:53:40.050 --> 00:53:41.108
Huh?


00:53:43.687 --> 00:53:47.453
You keep looking for trouble,
I will show it to you.
Do you hear me?


00:53:50.594 --> 00:53:52.585
Dana! Shit,
that was him!


00:53:53.863 --> 00:53:55.194
We have to
call the cops.


00:53:55.398 --> 00:53:59.357
Cops don't come to
the kasie! Dana. Dana!


00:54:00.103 --> 00:54:01.297
This is insane.


00:54:05.175 --> 00:54:08.576
Dana.
This is not worth it,
whatever it is.


00:54:09.012 --> 00:54:10.445
I just wanna see
where he goes,


00:54:10.513 --> 00:54:12.811
and we can come
back later for help.


00:54:12.882 --> 00:54:14.372
Come on.


00:54:24.661 --> 00:54:25.958
Dana.
What?


00:54:26.029 --> 00:54:27.724
You don't know
what you're dealing with.


00:54:27.797 --> 00:54:29.890
We have to
get out of here.
Shh!


00:54:38.308 --> 00:54:40.970
Pushy.
That's Grant's truck.


00:54:41.044 --> 00:54:43.444
Grant's never been anywhere
near this part of town.


00:54:43.713 --> 00:54:45.647
Now, let's go. Please.


00:54:45.715 --> 00:54:47.683
Pushy, look.


00:54:53.657 --> 00:54:55.318
Come on.


00:55:12.842 --> 00:55:14.503
Always be prepared, right?


00:55:18.315 --> 00:55:20.545
Come on.


00:55:32.562 --> 00:55:34.689
Oh, my God! Pushy.


00:55:34.764 --> 00:55:36.459
Look. He's coming.


00:55:36.533 --> 00:55:38.558
Let's go. Run!


00:55:38.868 --> 00:55:40.631
Hey! Get them!


00:55:40.704 --> 00:55:41.830
Get them!


00:55:41.905 --> 00:55:44.203
Come on, come on.


00:55:44.274 --> 00:55:46.674
Go, go. Go!


00:55:50.714 --> 00:55:52.841
If we make it through this,
I'm gonna kill you.


00:55:52.916 --> 00:55:54.508
Leave us alone!


00:56:01.791 --> 00:56:03.691
Look out!


00:56:06.229 --> 00:56:07.958
Come on, go!


00:56:13.002 --> 00:56:14.435
Jump! Jump!


00:56:21.544 --> 00:56:24.035
Well, you happy now?


00:56:24.114 --> 00:56:25.581
"Happy"? What do you mean?


00:56:25.849 --> 00:56:27.874
You know, I have to
live around here!


00:56:27.951 --> 00:56:30.385
You might wanna
think about that
once in a while!


00:56:30.453 --> 00:56:33.286
This is getting
out of control, Dana.


00:56:50.206 --> 00:56:52.504
Hey, come and get it.
It's firing.


00:56:53.443 --> 00:56:54.910
Where were you
last night?


00:56:55.044 --> 00:56:56.534
What?


00:56:57.647 --> 00:56:59.239
Out with a couple of
mates having a few.


00:57:00.183 --> 00:57:01.207
What are you, my wife?


00:57:02.285 --> 00:57:05.652
Funny,
'cause I saw your truck
in the Umlazi township.


00:57:06.389 --> 00:57:09.187
Umlazi?
Why would I go there?


00:57:09.526 --> 00:57:11.926
We saw your license
plate, Grant.


00:57:11.995 --> 00:57:14.395
We also saw what was
inside of your truck.


00:57:15.098 --> 00:57:17.225
I reported it
to the police.


00:57:25.875 --> 00:57:28.844
Used to have
a term for kooks


00:57:29.612 --> 00:57:32.877
who got in way
over their heads on
a big day at Supers,


00:57:34.951 --> 00:57:36.213
shark bait.


00:57:41.324 --> 00:57:42.416
I think I'll take
this one in.


00:57:45.061 --> 00:57:46.153
Yeah, you do that.


00:57:55.004 --> 00:57:57.234
You didn't call the cops.


00:57:57.307 --> 00:57:59.901
I bluffed.
And he didn't fold.


00:58:00.376 --> 00:58:02.640
I'm not done with this.


00:58:15.391 --> 00:58:18.451
She's 18.
She's my daughter.
I need to find her.


00:58:18.895 --> 00:58:20.419
Sir, she's an adult.


00:58:20.497 --> 00:58:24.058
We can put her photo in
our database and put out
a missing persons alert,


00:58:24.133 --> 00:58:26.567
but I'm afraid there's
not much else we can do.


00:58:26.870 --> 00:58:27.859
Next.


00:58:27.937 --> 00:58:29.734
Look, how do l
access the database?


00:58:31.708 --> 00:58:33.266
Next.


00:58:36.513 --> 00:58:41.280
I can't believe I let
that creep con me
into actually liking him.


00:58:41.351 --> 00:58:43.911
A guy so opposite to
everything I believe in!


00:58:46.923 --> 00:58:48.151
What's so funny?


00:58:49.092 --> 00:58:51.117
You're not that
different from Grant.


00:58:51.427 --> 00:58:53.952
What? What's that
supposed to mean?


00:58:56.199 --> 00:58:59.430
He's got a rich daddy.
You've got a rich daddy.


00:59:00.203 --> 00:59:04.503
Face it, you're both just
spoiled kids playing at
being surf bums for a while.


00:59:05.041 --> 00:59:06.975
And making trouble
for the rest of us.


00:59:07.043 --> 00:59:08.908
Where the hell is
this coming from?


00:59:09.279 --> 00:59:12.976
You think because
my father's rich that l
don't care about things?


00:59:13.049 --> 00:59:15.017
That I don't feel pain?


00:59:15.084 --> 00:59:16.881
You care about
what's important to you.


00:59:17.220 --> 00:59:18.847
What?
You're dangerous.


00:59:19.155 --> 00:59:20.986
And everyone else
gets dragged along
for the ride.


00:59:21.057 --> 00:59:23.218
Hey, you volunteered
for this ride, remember?


00:59:23.626 --> 00:59:26.151
Yeah, well, maybe
I'm getting off your bus.


00:59:26.596 --> 00:59:29.531
I'm sick and tired
of living someone
else's dream.


00:59:29.832 --> 00:59:31.322
This is your dream, too!


00:59:31.634 --> 00:59:35.229
Right. And we both know Tara
is not gonna let that happen.


00:59:38.541 --> 00:59:39.769
You're giving up?


00:59:41.978 --> 00:59:43.070
You're giving up?


00:59:43.580 --> 00:59:45.605
Just leave me alone, Dana.


00:59:51.421 --> 00:59:54.447
You know what?
Maybe Tara was
right about you!


00:59:55.325 --> 00:59:57.486
No commitment and no guts!


00:59:57.760 --> 01:00:00.024
Yeah? Thanks.


01:00:00.096 --> 01:00:01.188
No problem.


01:00:52.849 --> 01:00:54.316
Grant!


01:01:26.949 --> 01:01:28.280
Hey, Dana.
Hey.


01:01:30.186 --> 01:01:33.246
Well, I guess I need
a place to stay.
Just for one night.


01:01:33.423 --> 01:01:35.050
I'm headed to
J-bay tomorrow.


01:01:41.397 --> 01:01:42.523
You can
stay in our room.


01:01:42.598 --> 01:01:43.997
Yeah, the more
the merrier.


01:01:45.535 --> 01:01:47.093
Look, I think
it's your lucky day.


01:01:47.270 --> 01:01:50.171
This cowpoke was gonna
bunk with Flash and Pete
over in Tim's bus.


01:01:50.807 --> 01:01:54.140
Seems like a good opportunity
for you to, you know, do
some thinkin' up in my room.


01:01:55.144 --> 01:01:56.168
Thanks, Cowboy.


01:01:56.245 --> 01:01:58.008
Come on.
I'll help you
get set up.


01:01:59.082 --> 01:02:00.106
Thanks, guys.


01:02:00.216 --> 01:02:01.205
Have a good night.
Nice dreams.


01:02:01.884 --> 01:02:03.010
Sorry, boys.


01:02:03.086 --> 01:02:05.213
Hey,
if you change your mind,
I've got condoms.


01:02:05.321 --> 01:02:06.845
You know,
Tim says swell's comin'.


01:02:06.923 --> 01:02:08.788
Yeah, I guess.


01:02:08.858 --> 01:02:11.520
Shit, right in time
for the Roxy tryouts.


01:02:11.594 --> 01:02:13.858
I wonder if Tara's
really gonna be there.


01:02:13.930 --> 01:02:17.161
Yeah, I heard she left
earlier today with Grant,


01:02:17.233 --> 01:02:19.394
so I reckon
you ought to plan
on her being there.


01:02:19.469 --> 01:02:22.097
She left with Grant?
After all that?


01:02:22.939 --> 01:02:24.964
I don't think she knows.


01:02:26.109 --> 01:02:28.168
I mean, does any of us
really know what happened?


01:02:31.814 --> 01:02:34.282
Thanks for letting me
use your place.


01:02:34.350 --> 01:02:35.408
You got it.


01:02:42.625 --> 01:02:45.219
Dana! Dana!


01:02:50.166 --> 01:02:54.330
I'm out of time and I'm afraid
I'll never get back home.


01:02:54.904 --> 01:03:01.571
Dana. Dana? Dana,
where are you? Dana!


01:03:22.665 --> 01:03:25.600
Pushy.
Everybody, get up!


01:03:31.240 --> 01:03:32.400
Get up!


01:03:34.377 --> 01:03:35.810
Everybody, get up!


01:03:39.682 --> 01:03:40.740
Pushy!


01:03:44.287 --> 01:03:46.755
Everybody away
from the house now!


01:03:51.994 --> 01:03:53.825
Attention.
Pushy!


01:03:53.896 --> 01:03:57.297
The eThekwini Municipality,
by the order of the court,


01:03:57.366 --> 01:04:01.234
is hereby
demolishing this
condemned building.


01:04:01.304 --> 01:04:05.400
Any occupants
are hereby advised to
vacate immediately.


01:04:10.413 --> 01:04:11.437
Pushy!


01:04:18.754 --> 01:04:20.779
Pushy! Shit.


01:04:27.430 --> 01:04:28.624
Pushy!


01:04:32.835 --> 01:04:35.030
Damn it. Pushy!


01:04:35.104 --> 01:04:37.800
Everybody
move to open sand for
a head count. Go!


01:04:39.275 --> 01:04:40.970
Go. Come on, let's go.


01:04:42.645 --> 01:04:44.738
Pushy!
Dana, I'm here.


01:04:45.381 --> 01:04:46.541
I was looking for you.


01:04:54.557 --> 01:04:55.717
Go! Run! Come on!


01:04:55.791 --> 01:04:58.760
Pushy! Dana!
Come on! Come on!


01:05:07.737 --> 01:05:10.672
Holy shit!
There goes our home.


01:05:15.311 --> 01:05:18.747
Wait a minute. Tim.
Where's Tim?


01:05:18.948 --> 01:05:20.882
Tim!
Tim!


01:05:20.950 --> 01:05:22.611
Tim!
Tim!


01:05:26.422 --> 01:05:29.323
No way,
that thing runs!


01:05:36.232 --> 01:05:40.066
Attention. Unofficial vehicles
are not allowed on the beach.


01:06:09.632 --> 01:06:12.066
All aboard.
Who's coming aboard?


01:06:14.737 --> 01:06:17.399
Bus leaves in five minutes!
Where to?


01:06:17.707 --> 01:06:22.076
Jeffrey's Bay.
It's confirmed, swell of
the decade is on its way.


01:06:27.416 --> 01:06:28.940
Let's go to J-bay.


01:06:35.791 --> 01:06:37.452
Thanks for
coming after me.


01:06:38.461 --> 01:06:40.190
So, you going?


01:06:40.429 --> 01:06:42.989
You?
Only if you go.


01:06:45.101 --> 01:06:47.001
You never give up,
do you?


01:06:47.069 --> 01:06:48.127
Nope.


01:06:49.305 --> 01:06:50.738
Then hell, yeah,
I'm going.


01:06:51.741 --> 01:06:53.675
It's time you finished
your damn odyssey.


01:06:53.843 --> 01:06:58.109
You and me,
we've got an appointment
with destiny in J-bay.


01:06:58.180 --> 01:06:59.272
Hell, yeah, we do!


01:07:14.363 --> 01:07:15.853
Look after yourselves,
okay?


01:07:23.172 --> 01:07:24.503
Get on the bus, man!


01:07:40.656 --> 01:07:41.850
No way.


01:07:42.958 --> 01:07:44.619
You saved it all?


01:07:44.693 --> 01:07:45.717
Hell, yeah.


01:07:47.863 --> 01:07:50.457
Tim!
Hey, hey.


01:07:52.535 --> 01:07:54.162
I'm driving. Come on.


01:07:59.975 --> 01:08:01.602
Thank you.


01:08:54.330 --> 01:08:56.389
Come on! Dana, Pushy, run!
Get on the bus!


01:08:56.899 --> 01:08:58.298
Come on!
Move it!


01:10:20.316 --> 01:10:23.251
Hello. I'm looking
for my daughter.


01:10:23.652 --> 01:10:24.983
Her name's...
You're Dana's dad.


01:10:26.288 --> 01:10:28.347
Yeah. Is she...
Is she here?


01:10:28.824 --> 01:10:32.487
Nope. The whole family's
on the odyssey.
Chasing the swell, you know.


01:10:32.561 --> 01:10:33.789
Well, except us folks.


01:10:34.863 --> 01:10:36.455
Family? Odyssey?


01:10:36.532 --> 01:10:39.729
Mmm. They're headed
down to Jeffrey's Bay.


01:10:39.802 --> 01:10:41.235
But they got
three days on you.


01:10:41.637 --> 01:10:43.605
And Lord knows where
they'll take off after that.


01:10:45.074 --> 01:10:46.541
What's the fastest
way there?


01:10:46.609 --> 01:10:47.667
Airplane.


01:11:25.214 --> 01:11:26.806
Hey.


01:11:28.050 --> 01:11:29.517
Hey.


01:11:29.918 --> 01:11:31.180
You okay?


01:11:34.990 --> 01:11:36.548
Yeah.


01:11:38.127 --> 01:11:39.754
I'm good.


01:11:41.463 --> 01:11:44.398
You know,
we're technically
homeless now.


01:11:44.466 --> 01:11:46.058
Well, we still
have the bus.


01:11:46.135 --> 01:11:49.263
Yup, and a big, weird,
stinky family to fill it.


01:11:52.441 --> 01:11:54.466
Yeah.


01:11:54.910 --> 01:11:57.879
I'm just glad Pushy and l
are good again.
Yeah.


01:12:00.649 --> 01:12:02.844
Man, I hope
she makes that team.


01:12:03.419 --> 01:12:06.081
Tryouts are this Saturday,
that's two days away.


01:12:06.755 --> 01:12:07.881
Yeah.


01:12:10.392 --> 01:12:13.259
It's really great
how you supported her.


01:12:15.597 --> 01:12:18.225
You're a really
special person, Dana.


01:12:20.469 --> 01:12:23.370
Yeah? Do you wanna
write me a song about it?


01:12:25.207 --> 01:12:26.231
I already did.


01:12:26.308 --> 01:12:27.502
Oh, my God! You did?


01:12:27.576 --> 01:12:29.339
Yeah.
How's it go?


01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:32.613
It's complicated.


01:12:32.681 --> 01:12:33.943
No kidding.


01:12:35.250 --> 01:12:37.241
Come on,
let's hear it.


01:13:46.555 --> 01:13:48.386
It is.


01:13:49.558 --> 01:13:51.287
Yeah.


01:14:08.010 --> 01:14:09.034
Whoo!


01:14:09.111 --> 01:14:11.807
Go for it, Tim!


01:14:13.649 --> 01:14:15.116
Thank you.


01:14:34.436 --> 01:14:38.634
Okay, fasten your seatbelts,
hold on to your chickens,


01:14:38.707 --> 01:14:40.197
we flyin'.


01:16:06.562 --> 01:16:08.530
J-bay!


01:16:08.597 --> 01:16:10.087
Yeah!


01:16:18.840 --> 01:16:20.330
Wow.


01:17:08.357 --> 01:17:09.824
We made it.


01:17:09.891 --> 01:17:11.358
We did.


01:17:31.046 --> 01:17:35.574
Whoa. I can see why
your mom wanted to surf it.


01:17:35.651 --> 01:17:38.711
Why everyone
wants to surf it.
Yeah.


01:17:38.787 --> 01:17:41.779
But maybe it's a boy's
club for a reason.


01:17:41.857 --> 01:17:44.587
That wave is
a bone crusher.


01:17:45.861 --> 01:17:47.829
What's wrong?


01:17:49.364 --> 01:17:50.695
I don't know.


01:17:50.766 --> 01:17:53.633
I'm not afraid.
I'm gonna surf it
for my mom,


01:17:53.702 --> 01:17:57.035
but I just can't help feeling
that I'm missing something.


01:17:57.105 --> 01:17:58.436
Yeah?


01:18:01.109 --> 01:18:02.940
What do you think it is
that I'm searching for?


01:18:03.011 --> 01:18:05.172
Like, what do you
think this is about?


01:18:08.583 --> 01:18:10.983
I think you should
turn around.


01:18:11.386 --> 01:18:13.854
What? You mean go back?


01:18:14.389 --> 01:18:17.449
No, I mean turn around.


01:18:22.097 --> 01:18:23.325
Dad?


01:18:24.166 --> 01:18:25.633
Hey, Dana.


01:18:30.906 --> 01:18:34.000
Right. Well,
I'm gonna go.


01:18:34.076 --> 01:18:36.306
Give you guys some space.


01:18:45.787 --> 01:18:48.051
Tim. Tim.


01:18:48.390 --> 01:18:49.857
Dana's dad is here.


01:18:50.258 --> 01:18:52.419
Oh, wow.


01:18:54.062 --> 01:18:55.529
The hell I am!


01:18:55.597 --> 01:18:57.428
I am not going home.


01:18:57.499 --> 01:18:59.399
Dana, I came halfway
around the world...


01:18:59.468 --> 01:19:01.197
I didn't ask you to!


01:19:01.269 --> 01:19:03.328
I'm your father!
Yeah? Since when?


01:19:08.143 --> 01:19:11.408
Look, I know
you're going
through something,


01:19:12.080 --> 01:19:13.980
but you have your
future to consider.


01:19:14.116 --> 01:19:15.140
You have school
starting in the fall...


01:19:15.217 --> 01:19:16.241
No.


01:19:16.318 --> 01:19:20.152
That is your future,
that is your school.
It's not mine.


01:19:20.522 --> 01:19:22.080
So... So what?


01:19:23.091 --> 01:19:26.788
You're just going
to hang out here,
surfing and...


01:19:26.862 --> 01:19:29.353
I mean, Jesus, Dana,
what are you doing here?


01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:32.093
I mean, help me out here,
'cause I'm trying
to understand.


01:19:32.167 --> 01:19:34.101
I mean, you wanna be
like your mother,
is that it?


01:19:34.202 --> 01:19:35.635
Follow in her footsteps?


01:19:35.704 --> 01:19:37.638
I mean, let it go,
Dana. She's dead!


01:19:46.715 --> 01:19:49.013
Wow.


01:19:49.084 --> 01:19:51.450
You really have a way
with words, Dad.


01:19:51.520 --> 01:19:52.578
Dana, l...


01:19:58.360 --> 01:20:00.828
Go home.


01:20:00.896 --> 01:20:04.457
Just go home
and leave me
the hell alone!


01:20:08.737 --> 01:20:09.931
Dana...


01:20:16.111 --> 01:20:20.411
He thinks
that just by coming here,
it shows that he cares.


01:20:21.449 --> 01:20:24.475
Well, it does.


01:20:24.553 --> 01:20:26.145
Just saying.


01:20:29.724 --> 01:20:32.318
What, you too?


01:20:32.394 --> 01:20:36.490
You know,
what you're going through
is a really big deal.


01:20:38.333 --> 01:20:40.858
Whether you
realize it or not.


01:20:42.103 --> 01:20:44.435
You lost your mom.


01:20:44.506 --> 01:20:46.303
We're sorry about that.


01:20:47.742 --> 01:20:49.733
But are you ready to
lose your dad, too?


01:20:50.345 --> 01:20:51.744
What? No.
That's not what...


01:20:51.813 --> 01:20:54.077
Maybe it is.


01:20:55.450 --> 01:20:57.645
Maybe that's the missing
piece of the puzzle.


01:20:59.221 --> 01:21:01.815
Maybe that's why
you're really here,


01:21:02.691 --> 01:21:05.319
to figure out the rest
of the puzzle,


01:21:07.229 --> 01:21:09.754
before you lose that, too.


01:21:11.666 --> 01:21:13.759
Wow.


01:21:13.835 --> 01:21:15.632
Aren't you a smart boy.


01:21:17.639 --> 01:21:18.936
Not so smart.


01:21:24.312 --> 01:21:26.872
Hey, listen.


01:21:27.916 --> 01:21:30.476
Unmistakable party sounds.


01:21:30.552 --> 01:21:34.079
Hell, let's crash it.
I could use a distraction.


01:21:35.790 --> 01:21:37.587
It looks like there's
a lot of Roxy people.


01:21:38.159 --> 01:21:39.786
May be a chance to make
a good impression.


01:21:39.861 --> 01:21:41.419
I don't know
about this.


01:21:47.836 --> 01:21:49.303
Congratulations,
you made it.


01:21:49.371 --> 01:21:51.396
Yep. I'll take
that 100 now.


01:21:51.473 --> 01:21:54.101
Not just yet.
She still has to
surf Supertubes.


01:21:54.242 --> 01:21:55.300
I will.


01:21:55.377 --> 01:21:57.106
Change your mind
about trying out
for the team?


01:21:57.479 --> 01:21:59.640
Nope. And neither did Push.


01:22:02.450 --> 01:22:04.611
She'll be there.
Really?


01:22:06.454 --> 01:22:08.422
That I can't
wait to see.


01:22:11.760 --> 01:22:13.751
Really? What...


01:22:14.562 --> 01:22:16.154
How you doing?
How you doing?


01:22:21.569 --> 01:22:22.695
Crap. Come on.


01:22:26.908 --> 01:22:28.273
Hey, Grant.


01:22:30.378 --> 01:22:31.606
We need to talk.


01:22:31.680 --> 01:22:32.977
Man, you don't
wanna do this.


01:22:33.048 --> 01:22:34.515
People have told me things.


01:22:35.050 --> 01:22:36.950
I don't wanna
believe them.


01:22:37.018 --> 01:22:38.918
I wanna hear the truth
from my friend.


01:22:39.988 --> 01:22:41.353
What things?
What are you
talking about?


01:22:41.423 --> 01:22:43.220
Please, tell me
it isn't true, man.


01:22:43.425 --> 01:22:45.893
Tell me it isn't true
about the tusks.


01:22:47.429 --> 01:22:48.794
I'm outta here.
Answer the question!


01:22:48.930 --> 01:22:50.625
Is it true?


01:22:53.535 --> 01:22:55.230
Hey, hey, stop it!


01:22:55.303 --> 01:22:58.101
Back off. This is
between the two of them.


01:23:17.726 --> 01:23:19.853
Come on, guys,
that's enough.


01:23:20.528 --> 01:23:21.552
That's enough!


01:23:43.318 --> 01:23:44.376
Why?


01:23:48.757 --> 01:23:50.748
I needed the money, bro.


01:23:52.827 --> 01:23:54.954
I'm broke.


01:23:56.798 --> 01:23:59.062
I was just the middleman.


01:23:59.134 --> 01:24:01.432
I made a stupid mistake!


01:24:13.448 --> 01:24:14.915
What, so you...


01:24:15.183 --> 01:24:16.707
You bailing on me, too?


01:24:19.988 --> 01:24:21.853
Give me one good
reason I shouldn't.


01:24:31.366 --> 01:24:32.993
We know what it means and
we know what it takes,


01:24:33.234 --> 01:24:34.929
so to us you're all winners.


01:24:48.516 --> 01:24:50.177
I'm telling you,


01:24:50.251 --> 01:24:52.981
they're gonna recognize me
from last night.


01:24:53.054 --> 01:24:55.614
"There's that troublemaker."


01:24:55.690 --> 01:24:57.453
Pushy, be serious.


01:24:58.059 --> 01:24:59.890
They probably didn't
even notice us.


01:25:12.407 --> 01:25:13.704
Nice seeing you again.


01:25:14.075 --> 01:25:16.134
Thanks for ruining
the party last night.


01:25:16.211 --> 01:25:18.111
She's okay.
I know her.


01:25:21.916 --> 01:25:23.611
Seriously. She's cool.


01:25:27.722 --> 01:25:29.815
Okay.


01:25:29.891 --> 01:25:32.359
Put this on
over your wetsuit
and wait to be called.


01:25:34.195 --> 01:25:35.526
Thank you.


01:25:41.703 --> 01:25:43.034
So sorry.


01:25:47.809 --> 01:25:49.003
Sorry.


01:25:51.446 --> 01:25:53.778
Welcome, ladies,
to the Roxy team tryouts,


01:25:53.848 --> 01:25:56.874
here at Phantom Reef
in the surf town
of Jeffrey's Bay.


01:25:57.018 --> 01:25:59.509
It's one heat per girl,
two girls per heat.


01:25:59.687 --> 01:26:02.622
You go head-to-head,
and you only have 10 minutes.


01:26:02.690 --> 01:26:03.952
So, give it your best.


01:26:04.025 --> 01:26:06.493
And if that isn't
enough pressure,


01:26:06.561 --> 01:26:09.860
here to comment for us today,
straight from the world tour,


01:26:09.931 --> 01:26:13.731
Roxy's own Sally Fitzgibbons,
and Laura Enever.


01:26:15.470 --> 01:26:19.531
Hey, girls, I just wanna say
I know what it took for you
to be here today,


01:26:19.607 --> 01:26:21.472
because four years ago,
this was us.


01:26:21.743 --> 01:26:24.268
And make no mistake,
the competition's tough.


01:26:24.345 --> 01:26:27.746
Especially since
we're only looking for
one more Roxy team rider.


01:26:28.049 --> 01:26:31.849
By the end of today,
one of you is going
to be one of us.


01:26:35.823 --> 01:26:37.256
Let the games begin!


01:26:37.325 --> 01:26:39.691
Heat number one,
Savage and Nahoma.


01:26:42.096 --> 01:26:44.997
Heat number two,
Jackson and Dottie.


01:26:46.167 --> 01:26:49.000
Heat number three,
Hoffmeyer and Saville.


01:26:51.306 --> 01:26:53.206
Okay, next heat.


01:26:54.342 --> 01:26:56.810
Heat number four,
Cochran and Knotts.


01:27:00.014 --> 01:27:02.744
Weak backside.
You'd kick her ass.


01:27:09.524 --> 01:27:12.357
Okay, let's have
our final heat.


01:27:12.460 --> 01:27:14.690
Kamalo and Bahn,
you're up.
Okay.


01:27:16.397 --> 01:27:17.864
All you need is
one good ride.


01:27:18.399 --> 01:27:20.833
One, and you get
to keep that vest.


01:27:21.836 --> 01:27:23.064
Okay?
Let's do it.


01:27:23.137 --> 01:27:24.263
Okay.
Okay.


01:27:24.339 --> 01:27:26.603
Kamalo and Bahn,
let's go!


01:27:32.146 --> 01:27:33.579
Do me proud.


01:27:36.751 --> 01:27:38.946
Right, Pushy!
Go, Pushy!


01:27:40.888 --> 01:27:43.550
Come on, Pushy!
Come on!


01:27:44.559 --> 01:27:45.787
Yeah, Pushy!


01:28:10.118 --> 01:28:13.747
You know,
these girls worked so hard
and sacrificed so much.


01:28:13.821 --> 01:28:15.880
It takes real guts
just to be out there.


01:28:24.999 --> 01:28:26.899
That's gotta hurt!


01:28:35.343 --> 01:28:38.779
Looks like purple
needs to shake it off
and get back out there.


01:28:44.719 --> 01:28:47.654
Nice riding
for yellow, though.
Should be a good score.


01:28:48.323 --> 01:28:50.052
Okay, watch the outside.


01:28:50.124 --> 01:28:51.148
Come on.


01:28:57.865 --> 01:28:59.264
What's that?


01:29:01.736 --> 01:29:03.727
I remember this girl
from last year.


01:29:03.805 --> 01:29:04.999
Yeah, so do I.


01:29:05.206 --> 01:29:08.869
Only a handful of
black female surfers
have ever competed,


01:29:09.043 --> 01:29:11.978
so we're witnessing
a little piece of history
right now.


01:29:14.682 --> 01:29:15.979
How did you find this?


01:29:17.485 --> 01:29:21.979
Well, it turns out when Grant
found out it was your thing
that that guy stole, he...


01:29:22.056 --> 01:29:23.580
He knew?


01:29:23.658 --> 01:29:25.819
Only after
you found his truck
and yelled at him.


01:29:26.294 --> 01:29:30.060
But he took his sweet time
getting it back to you.


01:29:30.131 --> 01:29:31.792
Probably because
ofyou and Tim.


01:29:32.867 --> 01:29:35.893
You know,
male rivalry
and all that.


01:29:39.407 --> 01:29:40.965
You've
got one minute.


01:29:41.175 --> 01:29:42.767
One minute to go
in this heat.


01:29:43.077 --> 01:29:44.237
This is it.


01:29:44.312 --> 01:29:46.177
One minute to go
in this year's
Roxy team tryouts.


01:29:46.247 --> 01:29:47.737
Come on, Pushy!


01:29:49.550 --> 01:29:52.451
This is your time,
Pushy. Represent.


01:29:54.589 --> 01:29:55.647
She better get
her ass going.


01:29:55.923 --> 01:29:59.620
She's really going
to have to get moving to
get around this section.


01:29:59.994 --> 01:30:01.086
Come on.


01:30:12.607 --> 01:30:13.972
Come on, Pushy!


01:30:14.041 --> 01:30:16.839
Okay, surfer's in position.
She's paddling hard.


01:30:30.324 --> 01:30:31.848
Okay,
she's up and riding.


01:30:31.926 --> 01:30:33.257
What's she gonna do?


01:30:33.594 --> 01:30:34.618
Come on, Pushy.


01:30:52.747 --> 01:30:54.009
Oh, my God!


01:30:54.081 --> 01:30:55.343
Nice one.


01:31:15.403 --> 01:31:17.200
Oh, my God!
She did it!


01:31:25.346 --> 01:31:29.043
She pulled it off.
She did it! Yeah!


01:31:29.951 --> 01:31:33.250
Wow.
That was the best surfing
we've seen all day.


01:31:33.321 --> 01:31:34.845
Well, it took
a long time coming.


01:31:34.922 --> 01:31:38.790
Yeah, it was a slow start
by purple, but that aerial
really made up for it.


01:31:38.960 --> 01:31:40.518
We'll have to see what
the judges have to say.


01:31:40.795 --> 01:31:42.092
Wouldn't wanna be
in their seats.


01:31:42.163 --> 01:31:43.289
Everyone,
gather around.


01:31:43.364 --> 01:31:45.855
We're gonna
have an announcement in
about two minutes' time.


01:31:48.202 --> 01:31:49.226
You got it, okay?


01:31:51.772 --> 01:31:53.399
That was
a lekker ride.


01:31:53.708 --> 01:31:55.539
You need to work on
your consistency, though.


01:31:56.010 --> 01:31:58.410
And you need to
read the waves.


01:32:01.048 --> 01:32:04.279
So, we've got a big
decision to make here.


01:32:04.685 --> 01:32:06.346
It's okay,
you've got this.


01:32:06.454 --> 01:32:08.251
You killed it.
You killed it.


01:32:10.157 --> 01:32:13.786
What do you think?
So, we're thinking
there's only...


01:32:13.895 --> 01:32:17.092
Okay, ladies,
I know it's been
a tough competition.


01:32:17.565 --> 01:32:19.465
You should all
feel like winners.


01:32:19.534 --> 01:32:22.697
Unfortunately,
there's only one space
left on the Roxy team.


01:32:22.970 --> 01:32:25.530
And our overall
winner today


01:32:26.340 --> 01:32:27.739
is Pushy Kamalo.


01:32:40.121 --> 01:32:42.385
Pushy!
Pushy! Pushy! Pushy!


01:33:04.545 --> 01:33:07.946
So, welcome
to the team.


01:33:12.920 --> 01:33:14.945
What took you so long?


01:33:15.957 --> 01:33:17.754
Thank you.


01:33:26.567 --> 01:33:31.368
And I want to thank
all of my friends
for feeding the fire.


01:33:31.439 --> 01:33:32.531
Cheers.


01:33:32.974 --> 01:33:36.137
And I want to thank you
for keeping me going.


01:33:37.845 --> 01:33:39.312
Thank you.


01:33:56.063 --> 01:33:57.394
Will you guys give me
a few minutes?


01:33:59.467 --> 01:34:01.560
Take all the time you need.


01:34:09.477 --> 01:34:11.843
I'm so proud of you.


01:34:14.649 --> 01:34:17.777
So, do you
come here often?


01:34:18.552 --> 01:34:20.486
Once every 20 years or so.


01:34:24.759 --> 01:34:26.727
Can I show
you something?


01:34:45.813 --> 01:34:48.611
I'm sorry, I didn't
mean to upset you.


01:34:49.583 --> 01:34:51.642
No, it's just


01:34:52.987 --> 01:34:54.511
seeing these,


01:34:56.424 --> 01:34:58.483
it brings back memories.


01:34:59.960 --> 01:35:02.360
Your mother and l, we...


01:35:02.730 --> 01:35:06.063
We took the same trip
that summer we met.


01:35:06.701 --> 01:35:09.829
I know. That's why
I wanted to show you.


01:35:17.812 --> 01:35:20.975
I also wanted to apologize.


01:35:21.882 --> 01:35:24.442
I didn't mean
what I said last night.


01:35:26.220 --> 01:35:28.654
It's weird,


01:35:28.723 --> 01:35:30.623
but these past
couple of weeks


01:35:31.525 --> 01:35:35.086
I've learned what it means
to be part of a family.


01:35:35.896 --> 01:35:38.091
I understand.


01:35:39.667 --> 01:35:42.363
After your mom died,


01:35:44.105 --> 01:35:46.573
the truth is,
I couldn't handle it.


01:35:47.842 --> 01:35:50.538
I just... I shut down.


01:35:51.812 --> 01:35:53.803
I shut down when
you needed me the most.


01:35:56.117 --> 01:35:58.312
You did all right, Dad.


01:35:59.320 --> 01:36:02.448
You always found a way
to take care of me.


01:36:03.991 --> 01:36:06.050
Too much sometimes.


01:36:06.594 --> 01:36:08.255
I know.


01:36:08.329 --> 01:36:09.956
And I was wrong
about that, too.


01:36:11.532 --> 01:36:14.228
I tried to control you.


01:36:14.301 --> 01:36:17.099
I was just so afraid
of losing you.


01:36:18.739 --> 01:36:20.604
Just like I lost her.


01:36:23.377 --> 01:36:25.208
And now I've lost you both.


01:36:27.414 --> 01:36:28.972
You haven't lost me, Dad.


01:36:58.212 --> 01:37:00.009
I think it's time.


01:37:26.841 --> 01:37:29.173
You're home now, Mom.


01:37:44.925 --> 01:37:47.519
One more thing left to do.


01:39:27.328 --> 01:39:29.159
Hey, what's it like
out there?


01:39:29.229 --> 01:39:30.321
It's firing.


01:39:31.231 --> 01:39:32.289
Do you reckon
they'll let me in?


01:39:32.933 --> 01:39:34.093
Um...


01:39:34.168 --> 01:39:36.432
Yeah, I'm sure ifyou
show a little respect
you'll be fine.


01:39:38.238 --> 01:39:39.671
It's actually pretty
heavy out there.


01:39:39.740 --> 01:39:41.037
You sure you're in
the right place?


01:39:44.111 --> 01:39:45.578
Yeah, I'm sure.


01:39:45.646 --> 01:39:47.807
Okay, good luck.


01:39:48.148 --> 01:39:49.376
Thanks.


01:40:41.435 --> 01:40:42.766
Hey, locals only.


01:40:44.238 --> 01:40:46.536
No lifeguards here,
sweetheart.


01:40:47.174 --> 01:40:49.369
It's too hot for girls.
Seriously, get out of here.


01:40:50.144 --> 01:40:51.702
Just leave before
you kill yourself.


01:40:53.147 --> 01:40:55.308
All right, guys, guys.
Just chill, all right?


01:40:55.382 --> 01:40:57.942
Just let her through.
She's cool.


01:41:01.355 --> 01:41:02.413
Good luck.


01:41:03.657 --> 01:41:04.783
I'm outta here.


01:41:06.493 --> 01:41:08.154
Think you're tough?


01:41:13.400 --> 01:41:15.425
Hey, kiddie beach
is down the way.


01:41:15.502 --> 01:41:17.697
Go on, you don't belong
here. Get out of here.


01:41:17.771 --> 01:41:19.238
Just go home.


01:41:24.344 --> 01:41:26.141
Looks huge out there.


01:41:26.613 --> 01:41:28.080
Yeah.


01:41:29.817 --> 01:41:31.011
This is it.


01:41:34.555 --> 01:41:35.988
Where is she?


01:41:39.893 --> 01:41:42.020
Oh, shit.


01:41:44.198 --> 01:41:46.598
I mean, she'll be fine.


01:41:49.336 --> 01:41:51.065
I think.


01:41:56.210 --> 01:41:58.678
Let's go up top.
Better view.


01:43:24.364 --> 01:43:25.729
Hey, you okay?


01:43:25.799 --> 01:43:27.061
Watch the waves.


01:43:27.134 --> 01:43:28.726
You're tougher
than you look.


01:43:31.505 --> 01:43:34.303
When you go, go.
Don't hesitate.
Go for it.


01:43:54.027 --> 01:43:55.824
Come on,
you can do this.


01:43:57.598 --> 01:44:00.396
Go for it,
you can do it.


01:44:16.550 --> 01:44:18.643
Man, she's got it.


01:45:55.716 --> 01:45:56.876
Whoo!


01:46:30.117 --> 01:46:31.141
Yes!


01:46:33.687 --> 01:46:36.383
Looked pretty
free-spirited to me.


01:46:38.825 --> 01:46:40.315
Did you get
what you wanted?


01:46:51.171 --> 01:46:52.468
Yeah.


01:46:55.008 --> 01:46:56.032
I'm so proud of you.


01:46:56.610 --> 01:46:57.634
Thanks, Dad.


01:46:57.711 --> 01:46:59.338
Your mom would
have been, too.


01:50:39.265 --> 01:50:40.664
Hit us with it, Cowboy.


01:50:47.474 --> 01:50:49.408
Wait, tell us
what she was doing.


01:51:56.843 --> 01:51:57.832
Oh!


01:52:17.464 --> 01:52:18.726
Shut up!
Shut up!

